law.text:
		Every resident who applies for a license to take or catch oysters and clams shall pay as follows or as subsequently revised by the Commission pursuant to § 28.2-201:

For each person taking or catching oysters by hand or with ordinary tongs, $10;


For each single-rigged patent tong boat taking oysters, $35;


For each double-rigged patent tong boat taking oysters, $70;


For each person taking or catching clams by hand or with ordinary tongs, $15;


For each single-rigged patent tong boat taking clams, $35;


For each double-rigged patent tong boat taking clams, $70; and


For each dredge used for taking or catching clams, $50.
